// @hint redundant type annotation: `c` is inferred as `{r: i32}`
// The annotations that draw those hints are the CELL: `c`/`lc`/`c0`/`s0` must be the ARM
// nominally, not the inferred structural `{r: i32}` — deleting them to silence the hint
// would delete the defect. Declared, per the fixture rule.
// D197 — the closure-FIELD rung of D195: `holder.go(c)`, where `go` is a closure-valued
// field and the call's result is a union ARM.
//
// `exprVariantIndex`'s `Call` arm had no `Member`-callee leg at all, where its nullable
// twin `nulVariantIdxOfExpr` reads `fieldClosureFeOfRecv` → `cloRetValKind` /
// `cloRetValSlot`. `Dot` is the arm's layout twin, so the miss was silent: the cell took
// Dot's `sHeapIdx` heap while the call returns the arm's `uVarHeap` one.
//
// KEPT SEPARATE FROM `arm-through-closure-value-call.vl` DELIBERATELY. A `{ go: … }`
// literal beside a SECOND lambda in the same union program is a different, still-open
// hole (D199, `object literal is missing a union-variant field`) — folding the two into
// one file would make this fixture pin that hole instead of this rung.
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Dot = { r: i32 } // the arm's exact layout twin
type Circle = { r: i32 }

const c: Circle = { r: 7 }
const holder = { go: (x: Circle) => x }
const viaField = holder.go(c)
print(viaField.r)
